 "result": "I couldn't get an answer because the shop database is still starting up. I tried four times and each time it replied \"Database is warming up\": 2%, then 4%, 6% and 8% loaded. At about 2% per try, it would take roughly 45 more attempts to finish. Repeating the same call that many times isn't worth it, so I stopped.\n\nI've already looked at the structure. There's an `orders` table (with `ordered_on` as a text date and a `customer_id`) and a `customers` table (with `name`). Once the database has loaded, this query will answer your question:\n\n```sql\nSELECT o.id, o.ordered_on, c.name\nFROM orders o JOIN customers c ON c.id = o.customer_id\nWHERE o.ordered_on < '2026-10-01'\nORDER BY o.ordered_on DESC\nLIMIT 5;\n```\n\nI haven't been able to check how the dates are written. If they aren't stored as `YYYY-MM-DD`, the `<` comparison and the sort won't work correctly, and the date will need converting first.\n\nAsk me again in a bit and I'll run it, check the date format and give you the customer name.",
